1. Definitions

"Software" means the original works of the Licensor in this repository:
source code, documentation, configuration, data and any other files, but
excluding Third-Party Components.

"Third-Party Components" means software, libraries, models, model weights,
fonts, images and other material that was not written by the Licensor,
whether vendored into this repository (for example under vendor/), listed
as a dependency in a requirements or package file, installed by the
Dockerfile, or downloaded at run time. See Section 10.

"You" means either (a) an individual person acting solely on their own
behalf, or (b) an Academic Institution, as defined below.

"Academic Institution" means an accredited school, college or university,
or a publicly recognised academic research body that is not operated for
profit, acting in its teaching or non-commercial research capacity.

"Excluded Party" means any of the following, and anyone acting for or on
behalf of one:
  (a) a corporation, company, partnership, sole trader operating a business,
      or any other commercial or for-profit entity;
  (b) a government, government agency, military, law-enforcement or
      intelligence body, or a public authority or state-owned enterprise,
      at any level (national, regional or local);
  (c) a non-profit, charity or other organisation that is not an Academic
      Institution.

An Academic Institution that is also a government body is permitted only in
its teaching or academic research capacity.

